---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Bonded Seals for Threaded BSPP Adapters | Smokeless Heat Blog" description="There are various methods which can be used to seal the threaded adapters which you may find in the boiler delivery.">
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-24">
    <section class="py-16 bg-charcoal text-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="text-ember text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4">Installation</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl">Bonded Seals for Threaded BSPP Adapters</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="py-16 bg-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 space-y-6 text-charcoal/90 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          There are various methods that can be used to seal the threaded adapters that may come with the boiler. This post shows three effective methods to get that first joint tight. However, it is also possible to get an effective seal without the adapters by using 7 wraps of Teflon tape (we like Monster brand), then applying pipe dope over the Teflon, or by using Loctite 55 for that first joint.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-darkwood mt-8">1. Hemp and Paste</h2>
        <p>
          The Loctite video below shows both the Loctite product and the hemp-and-paste method side by side. We stock the hemp-and-paste product if you prefer that method.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-darkwood mt-8">2. Loctite 55</h2>
        <p>
          Loctite 55 can easily be purchased on Amazon or eBay. It is not typically found in North American plumbing supply stores.
        </p>

        <div class="aspect-video w-full mt-4">
          <iframe 
            width="100%" 
            height="100%" 
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/JC4fvZF-M-g" 
            title="Loctite 55 and hemp and paste" 
            frameborder="0" 
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" 
            allowfullscreen
            class="rounded border border-wood/20"
          ></iframe>
        </div>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-darkwood mt-8">3. Bonded Seals</h2>
        <p>
          This method is very easy. Simply push the washer-like seal over the threads and turn the adapter in until it bottoms out and becomes tight. The joints from that point on can be sealed with your favorite method, such as Teflon tape.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
          <img src="/images/IMG_0854-rotated-e1637006950928-300x225-1.jpg" alt="Bonded seal on adapter" class="w-full border border-wood/20" />
          <img src="/images/IMG_0856-300x225-1.jpg" alt="Bonded seal installed" class="w-full border border-wood/20" />
        </div>

        <div class="aspect-video w-full mt-4">
          <iframe 
            width="100%" 
            height="100%" 
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/H1GMgaV64-U" 
            title="Bonded seals installation" 
            frameborder="0" 
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" 
            allowfullscreen
            class="rounded border border-wood/20"
          ></iframe>
        </div>

        <p>
          These bonded seals can be purchased from the Discounthydraulichose.com website. Search for the part on their website.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.discounthydraulichose.com/" class="text-ember hover:underline" target="_blank">Discount Hydraulic Hose</a>
        </p>

        <p>
          Four bonded seal sizes are needed for the various threaded ports found on the boiler and tanks.
        </p>

        <img src="/images/bonded-seal-sizes-420x360-1.png" alt="Bonded seal sizes" class="w-full border border-wood/20" />

        <p>
          If you plan to use the built-in cooling coil, you will need a special thermostatic valve. These are the adapters for the copper cooling coil connection. The thermostat valve is purchased separately.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.discounthydraulichose.com/" class="text-ember hover:underline" target="_blank">Discount Hydraulic Hose</a>
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-wood mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-wood/20">
          Originally published: October 2022
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
